From cd583fcf1246e962c192ae195018218438d2ba53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 05:01:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08136/11362] [outer-loop] Apply adversarial corrections: the
 refinement null is a BROKEN INSTRUMENT, not a measured zero

Both reviews HOLD. Every disputed number re-derived from the shards independently.

The finding was that cell-level feedback improved an engine 0 of 160 times, read as
a clean null closing the last ARC induction lead. That reading is withdrawn.

What the omitted prefix_accuracy channel shows: induce reaches prefix>0 in 28/88
(up to 1.0); refactor in 4/160, capped at 0.125 (Fisher OR 18.2, p=1.03e-10).
15 cells collapse from a PERFECT prefix 1.0 to 0.0. The refactor step does not
fail to improve the engine -- it destroys its fit on the rows it was handed with
the answers.

Mechanism identified (neither reviewer had it): degenerate-identity collapse.
n_engine_snapshots == n_emitted in 117/117, so modules import and run; the
residue is identity stubs and raisers. results/arc_e3/ft09/world_model.py is a
structural identity function -- eight branches, every one `return grid`. The same
signature appears in the git trajectories (all 4 games peak then collapse to 0.0,
with IndexError/TypeError/NameError raisers and wrong_cells == true_changed_cells
identity rows) and in arc_llm_reinduction.py's own replay (0.65 -> 0.15 -> 0.075).

Harness defect found while verifying: exp5766's CEGIS round 0 IS single-shot, and
scores heldout>0 on 2/13 games (0.0598) where matched single-shot exp5764 scores
12/13 (0.3785) -- same model, same roster, same window builder. 6.33x. Its own
docstring cites 5764 as baseline; the gap was never flagged.

Also corrected: game-clustered test had zero power (10/13 games pinned at 0.0, so
min reachable p was 0.25, exactly the p reported); -0.3187 is single-shot vs
single-shot (best_achieved is identically round0); prior-art citation inverted
(the block concludes "store defect, not a proposer defect"); shards predate
retention (2026-07-29) and plannability (2026-07-31); slim_rounds drops the
crash-vs-wrong discriminator; identity control vacuous (n_noop=0).

Append-only: 30 and 42 prior keys byte-identical, none dropped, order preserved.
No default flipped, no solve claimed, nothing submitted, evidence dirs untouched.

